    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "FOR SALE BY ONLINE AUCTION FRI 9TH OCT @ 14:30PM\r\nRegister at https://keaneauctioneers.com/online-auctions/ and click on Offr tab in the bottom right corner\r\n\r\nProperty Summary:\r\nThis is a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity to acquire your dream home by the sea in the much-loved coastal village of Cullenstown, where the shoreline is quite literally on your doorstep and spectacular coastal views provide a constant backdrop to everyday life. The accommodation comprises a welcoming entrance hall leading to a comfortable living room and practical kitchen/dining area, complemented by a separate utility room, a well-appointed bathroom and an additional shower room. To the rear, the sun porch makes the most of the exceptional coastal setting, capturing views across Cullenstown and towards the sweeping Bannow shoreline. While the property would benefit from some upgrading, its exceptional setting isundoubtedly its greatest asset. Sea views, coastal scenery and the ever-present sound of the ocean combine to create a truly special place to call home. Outside, a detached garage and large garden offer excellentpotential, with ample scope for landscaping, outdoor living or future enhancement, subject to the necessary planning permissions.Cullenstown is surrounded by some of South Wexford’s finest natural amenities, including Cullenstown Strand, Bannow Island, Blackhall Strand and Ballyteigue Burrow. The nearby villages of Duncormick, Kilmore Quay and Our Lady’s Island, together with Wexford Town, are all within easy reach. A property in such a spectacular coastal setting is a rare find, making this an exciting opportunity to create a wonderful seaside home in one of South Wexford's most cherished locations. Viewing is highly recommended."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hall - (8.79m x 1.16m),  Tiled flooring.\r\nLiving Room - (4.25m x 3.62m),  Laminate flooring, coving, stove with brick surround, archway to sunroom.\r\nSunroom 1 - (3.95m x 2.37m),  Tiled flooring, large windows with views of the beach, access to living room, sliding doors to Sunroom 2\r\nSunroom 2 - (5.01m x 2.36m), Tiled flooring, door to patio area with view of coastline.\r\nShower Room - (1.80m x 1.95m),  WC, WHB, shower, tiled flooring.\r\nKitchen/Diner - (3.91m x 3.90m),  Eye & Waist level units, tiled flooring and part tiled walls, plumbed for appliance.\r\nUtility Room - (1.86m x 1.95m),  plumbed for appliances, tiled flooring, shower room off;\r\nBedroom 1 - (3.23m x 3.22m),  - Laminate flooring, built in wardrobes, coving.\r\nBedroom 2 - (4.09m 3.86m),  Laminate flooring, bult in wardrobes, WHB, coving.\r\nBedroom 3 - (3.23m x 2.93m),  Laminate flooring, built in wardrobes, coving.\r\nBedroom 4/Dining Room - (3.98m x 3.11m),  Carpet flooring, coving & centre rose.\r\nBathroom - (3.29m x 2.41m),  WC, WHB, bath, tiled flooring.\r\n\r\nOutside: Parking to the front, large rear garden, detached garage with \u001fat roof and double doors to front.\r\nServices: Electricity, mains water, private sewerage, oil \u001dred central heating.\r\nBER: E Ber No: 119673507 Performance indicator: 283.98 Wh/m2/yr"
